                    <death when="1000-01-01"/>
                    <occupation>Coal Merchant</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Samuel Etheridge Acton apprenticed 1747 to Robert Marram, Pewterers Co.
                            and received a premium of £21. Samuel Etheridge Acton, bachelor, married
                            Ann Wright, spinster, by Archbishop’s license on 25 December 1764 in St
                            Margaret Lothbury. Their witnesses were Wm Acton and Ann Wright. They
                            had a son, Samuel, who was baptised 19 April 1773 at St Mary Aldermary
                            The trades directories from 1776 to 1791 listed Samuel Acton as a coal
                            merchant of 9 Distaff Lane, Friday Street. The trades directory of 1777
                            listed Samuel Acton as a merchant of 82 Watling Street. </p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>

